# WattWise API boundary

- Read `docs/api.md` and the matching Zod schemas / Rust types before changing request or response shapes.
- `GET /api/risk` uses `county_fips` only (Harris `48201` supported). Coverage uses the disclosed Houston reference weather point — not county-wide aggregation or grid telemetry.
- `mode` is `weather_index` or `unavailable`. Index is 0–9 or null; scale 9 or null. Preserve assessment/fetch/expiry/window timestamps.
- `POST /api/plan`: answers are `yes` | `no` | `unknown` | `prefer_not_to_answer`. Server owns eligibility, priorities, and action text.
- Fixtures under `tests/fixtures` are synthetic test data, never live forecasts. Frontend tests parse the same files.
- Shared-module edits (`api.ts`, `risk.rs`, `plan.rs`, `main.rs`, API docs) require explicit teammate coordination. Prefer UI-only changes on the presentation branch.
